# Arm/disarm sensor-triggered auto-run. The sensor is mounted on the TCP, so a
# reading is trusted ONLY while the arm is idle and parked at home (near the parts):
# a part seen there runs one full pass through all saved points, then the arm returns
# home and waits for the next part. Readings taken mid-pass (sensor in the air) are
# ignored. Only runs while the servo is ON (a human enables the servo; auto-run never does).
bool enable
int32 input_bit     # input to watch, 0-15; -1 = keep the current/default (IN1, TCP sensor)
---
bool success
string message
